<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina places 91-, 364-day treasury bills.</title>
<headline>Argentina places 91-, 364-day treasury bills.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina Tuesday placed 250 million pesos in 91-day Letes Treasury bills at a cut-off yield of 6.10 percent and 500 million pesos in 364-day bills at 6.80 percent, the Economy Ministry said.</p>
<p>There were 49 bids on the 91-day bills for a bid-to-cover ratio of 3.69 times and 87 bids on the 364-day bills for a bid-to-cover ratio of 3.17 times.  </p>
<p>The price at the cut-off yield on the 91-day bills was 984,581 and the price on the 364-day bills was 931,244.</p>
<p>Market makers will be offered up to 10 percent more of both issues until 1730 local/2030 GMT Tuesday.</p>
<p>Settlement is due on March 21.</p>
<p>((--Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668))</p>
